  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1125 AM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nStrong high pressure systems will be centered off to our \nsoutheast and out to our west. We will experience relatively weaker\nridging in between. This means a very warm and humid pattern with\ndaily chances for showers and storms. It is nearly impossible to \nbe precise about rain hitting any particular location. Sadly, many\nspots will not get much rain at all through the next week while \na few spots get too much. In general, Sunday through Tuesday look\nlike the days with lowest rain coverage (10 to 30 percent) and \nhottest conditions as the 2 high pressure centers bridge together \nacross the area. The ridge will weaken over our area mid to late \nweek, allowing daily storm chances to increase (30 to 60 percent).\n\nMost days will bring heat index values over 100 for areas west of\nthe Plateau. The hottest days, Sunday through Tuesday, could see\nheat index values topping 105 for some spots. This will push the \nHeat Risk level to 3 out of 4 for many areas and advisories may \nbe considered.",
